-- title:
--   Faithful diamond action on the q-expansion field of X_H(M)
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field of characteristic zero, let $M$ be a nonzero natural number and let $H$ be a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$. Write $F_\Gamma =$ [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC K Γ`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101) for the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $K((q))$ obtained by adjoining to $K$ all quotients $\mathrm{intSeriesC}_K(p_f)/\mathrm{intSeriesC}_K(p_g)$ arising from two modular forms $f,g$ of a common weight $k$ for $\Gamma$ (regarded as a subgroup of $GL(2,\mathbb{R})$) together with integral power series $p_f,p_g$ representing their $q$-expansions, subject to $\mathrm{intSeriesC}_K(p_g)\neq 0$. Here $\Gamma$ is taken to be either [`CohCarrier.GammaH M H`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133), the image in $SL(2,\mathbb{Z})$ of the set of $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M)$ whose lower-right entry reduces mod $M$ to an element of $H$, or $\Gamma_0(M)$ itself. The assertion is that there exists a group homomorphism $\rho$ from $\Gamma_0(M)$ to the group of $K$-algebra automorphisms of $F_{\Gamma_H}$ such that: first, for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M)$, $\rho(\gamma)$ fixes every element of $F_{\Gamma_H}$ whose underlying Laurent series lies in $F_{\Gamma_0(M)}$; and second, for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M)$, $\rho(\gamma)$ is the identity automorphism if and only if the unit [`CohCarrier.gamma0Units M γ`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L121) (the reduction mod $M$ of the lower-right entry of $\gamma$) lies in the subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ generated by $H$ and $-1$.
--
--   This is the statement that the diamond operators of the covering $X_H(M)\to X_0(M)$ act on the $q$-expansion function field over the $\Gamma_0(M)$-field with kernel exactly $\pm\Gamma_H(M)$, so that $\Gamma_0(M)/\pm\Gamma_H(M)\cong(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times/\langle H,-1\rangle$ acts faithfully. It is used in the construction of full-level models, where an invariant semiring action on a base-changed Laurent series field is produced together with the identification of $j$ and the coordinate $x_H$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_monoidHom_gamma0_algEquiv_qExpFunctionFieldC_gammaH_apply_eq_one_iff_of_charZero.lean

